FESEM images of Figure 3a and b display the morphologies of ZIF-67 after carbonation (c-ZIF-67), which keeps the geometrical polyhedral shape. However, Figure 3b obviously indicates that the surfaces of c-ZIF-67 changes into rough surfaces compared with the precursor ZIF-67 (Figure S4). In addition, Figure 3c displays TEM image of MDPC, which still keeps the geometrical polyhedral shape after Co removal. Figure 3d reveals that there are plenty of pores and a small amount of residual Co exists in porous carbon matrix (black small spots in TEM figures). After encapsulated into Se, the Se/MDPC composite keeps the structure of MDPC as is shown in Figure 3e, f and g. It can be seen that the distribution of element Se is uniform from Figure S5. TEM image display in figure 3h further demonstrates that the perfectly diffusion of Se into the inside of abundant pores of MDPC, which is in favor of latter electrochemical performances.
